# The domain eras the post-deploy check accepts as "the era that should be
# running", one era id per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are
# ignored. While no era is listed the check only verifies that the host reports
# one, and does not compare it.
#
# Changing the era on a roll:
#   1. Add the NEW era id below and merge that BEFORE the roll, so a scheduled
#      check does not fail the moment the new era boots.
#   2. Roll. The check then passes on the new era.
#   3. Once the roll has settled, delete the OLD era id, so a rollback to it, or
#      a fork of the journal back onto it, fails the check instead of passing.
#
# The id is what the host reports at GET /version, the same id the era mint
# prints. Compare a live host with this file:
#
#   hecks check_era host=https://host.example expected=expected-era --wait
#   make check-era URL=https://host.example
